-- chem/cover.hypercubical — the electron and the flux it draws, as one walker. A nucleus of charge +1 sits at vertex 0
-- of a graph and an electron of charge −1 at a vertex v; the flux n puts a whole number on every line and Gauss's law
-- reads div n = δ₀ − δ_v. The electron's hop along a line carries the U(1) holonomy of that line, so it moves the
-- flux on the line by one (`cv-step`): the state after a walk is the vertex reached and the walk's chain, each line
-- counted with its direction. Two walks give one state exactly when their chains agree, so the states are the
-- vertices of the graph's largest abelian cover, the hop is the hop on that cover, and the electric energy Σ n² is a
-- potential on it. Checked: Gauss's law after every walk of up to four steps on the hexagon and up to three on the
-- smallest cage of the diamond net (`cv-gauss`); there and back is the start and once round the hexagon is not
-- (`cv-round`); on the hexagon after s steps one way, 6 Σ n² = s² + d(6 − d), d the remainder of s by 6
-- (`cv-well`): the walker on the line in a well, chem/fluxsplit.hypercubical's identity read along the cover.
-- A leaf: no module imports it.
import "fluxsplit.hypercubical"

